          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"undset-kristin-lavransdatter-c0bed71c8c4081a9\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.99,\"analysis\":\"Ragnfrid directly avows to Kristin that she loved her no less than Lavrans did. The clause is a retrospective presentation of her enduring maternal emotional state as true. It neither undertakes a new relational commitment nor functions as a reflex-like affective discharge: despite her tears, the narration explicitly describes her face and voice as calm.\",\"ambiguity\":null},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Ragnfrid speaks directly to her daughter Kristin within represented dialogue: «jeg elsket dig» (“I loved you”), embedded in an appeal to God and the Virgin Mary as witnesses.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"After Kristin suggests that her mother suspects pregnancy, Ragnfrid strikes her and then explains the painful history of their emotional distance. She acknowledges that Kristin may have believed herself less loved than she was by her father and counters this with a solemn maternal avowal. Her tears and the invocation of divine witnesses intensify and authenticate the claim, while the explicitly calm delivery weighs against expressive/reflexive force. The speech also seeks understanding and relational repair, but the core clause remains an avowal rather than an undertaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"«Men det vet Gud og jomfru Maria, at jeg elsket dig nok ikke mindre end Lavrans gjorde.»\",\"supports\":\"Strong truth-conditional force: Ragnfrid solemnly presents her past and continuing maternal love as a fact, comparing it with Lavrans’s love.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"E2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Ragnfrid says Kristin may have believed «at ikke jeg elsket dig saa meget — ikke slik som far din elsker dig».\",\"supports\":\"The utterance explicitly corrects Kristin’s presumed belief that her mother loved her less, confirming an avowal/report function.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"E3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"«Taarerne randt nedover Ragnfrids kinder, men hendes ansigt var ganske rolig og hendes stemme ogsaa.»\",\"supports\":\"Although affect is intense, the calm face and voice provide no positive evidence that the words themselves are a reflex-like expressive discharge; E therefore remains unsupported.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"E4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Ragnfrid recounts nursing the infant Kristin, fearing she would lose her, and feeling unable to rejoice because of her continual grief.\",\"supports\":\"The detailed retrospective explanation grounds the clause in reflective testimony about a longstanding maternal state rather than a new commitment or spontaneous verbal reflex.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"E5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is marked KEEP with reason VALID_EXPLICIT_LOVE_I_YOU and confidence 0.99.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms that the highlighted wording is an explicit first-person love predication addressed to the loved person.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core retrospective avowal. The emotional and reparative setting is adequately represented as context; it creates no residual pressure for P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
      ],
